IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Terms and Conditions Governing UOB Visa Signature Card`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. uob-visa-signature-tnc: "Terms and Conditions Governing UOB Visa
-- Signature Card", "Updated 28 October 2025 (Ver 2.1)" (United Overseas Bank
-- Limited), cl.1-4. The guidance FAQ (uob-visa-signature-faq) explains the
-- transition to separate caps; it ends in September 2025 and changes no rule
-- this module answers for.
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS.
--   cl.1(i)    UNI$1 per S$5 on the Card, no cap: the basic tier.
--   cl.1(ii)-(iii) SimplyGo (ABT) fares: UNI$1 per S$5 accumulated monthly; "With
--              effect from 1 July 2025, SimplyGo (ABT) Transactions shall
--              constitute Contactless Transactions", which earn UNI$10.
--   cl.1(iv)   What earns nothing (Excluded Transactions).
--   cl.2(i)    OVERSEAS SPEND: UNI$10 per S$5 "spend overseas or online in
--              foreign currencies (including card-not-present transactions ...)"
--              subject to a minimum Overseas Spend of S$1,000 per statement
--              period. "Card transactions made overseas but effected in
--              Singapore dollars will be treated as transactions in Singapore
--              dollars and will earn UNI$1 per S$5 spend. Online transactions
--              effected in Singapore dollars or in foreign currencies at
--              merchants with payment gateway in Singapore will also earn UNI$1."
--   cl.2(ii)   PETROL SPEND: UNI$10 per S$5 at MCC 5541/5542, excluding SPC and
--              Shell service stations.
--   cl.2(iii)  CONTACTLESS: UNI$10 per S$5 for the Card via Visa payWave, and
--              Apple Pay, Google Pay, Samsung Pay, Android Pay, UOB Mighty "at
--              any Visa payWave Readers, either by tapping or waving"; it excludes
--              Magnetic Secure Transmission and SPC transactions.
--   cl.2 (the [NEW] block, for cards approved on or after 1 July 2025
--              immediately, and for earlier cards from the September 2025
--              statement): Petrol Spend and/or Contactless: a combined minimum
--              of S$1,000 in Singapore dollars per statement period, UNI$10
--              capped at UNI$2,400 per statement period; Overseas Spend: a
--              minimum of S$1,000 per statement period, UNI$10 capped at
--              UNI$2,400; "treated as separate categories. Each category has
--              its own minimum spend requirements and separate bonus UNI$ cap."
--              "The UNI$10 consists of the basic UNI$1 earned plus an additional
--              of 9 bonus UNI$."
--   cl.4(i)    "the final UNI$ awarded for each transaction will be rounded down
--              to the nearest whole figure."
-- UNI$2,400 at UNI$10 per S$5 is S$1,200 of spend per category.
--
-- THE FLOOR IS A MONTH-END CONDITION. Below the S$1,000 minimum "to earn UNI$10"
-- no bonus is earned on any of the category's spend that statement period.
-- While the period's spend including this purchase is under S$1,000 the module
-- gives the basic tier as the floor, the bonus as the ceiling, and names the
-- condition. Once it is over, the bonus is certain.
--
-- THE FORKS.
--   F-uob-per-five: floor on whole S$5 blocks, ceiling pro rata.
--   F-vs-overlap: a foreign-currency tap overseas is both Overseas Spend and a
--     Contactless Transaction. The text does not say which category counts it.
--     The module takes the poorer pot's answer as the floor and the richer as the
--     ceiling and names the open reading.
--   F-bill-payments: floor 0 for a bill paid directly on the card.
-- THE VINTAGE. cl.2 gives cards approved before 1 July 2025 the combined
-- UNI$4,000 cap until the September 2025 statement. Every statement now open is
-- on the separate-cap structure for every card, so the vintage field of the
-- cardholder is not read.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.1(iv) -- what earns nothing`

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Visa Signature excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4829, 4900, 5199, 5960, 5965, 5993, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513, 6529, 6530, 6534,
         6540, 7349, 7511, 7523, 7995, 8062, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398, 8651, 8661,
         8699, 8999, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405

GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`VS cl.1(iv) excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN FALSE

GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`VS cl.1(iv)(e) lists the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `AXS`                                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FlashPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NETS VCashCard`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TRANSIT`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Razerpay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SingPost-SAM`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `iPayMy`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmoovPay`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal Bizconsulta or Capitalroya or Oandaasiapa`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Moneybookers`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Skrill`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `OANDA`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Saxo`                                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `IG Markets`                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SkyFX`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Banc de Binary`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `RWS-Levy`                                             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `NORWDS`                                               THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                        FALSE

-- cl.1(iv)(c): "all transactions or payments made to SPC Service Stations and
-- Shell Service Stations".
GIVEN seller IS A Merchant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`VS cl.1(iv)(c) excludes the merchant` seller MEANS
    seller EQUALS `SPC service station` OR seller EQUALS `Shell service station`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Visa Signature excludes the purchase` p MEANS
    `VS cl.1(iv) excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the code is among` p `the Visa Signature excluded category codes`
    OR `VS cl.1(iv)(e) lists the description` (p's descriptor)
    OR `VS cl.1(iv)(c) excludes the merchant` (p's merchant)
    OR p's `later reversed`


§§ `cl.2 -- which category a purchase is in`

-- Overseas Spend: a foreign-currency charge whose merchant's payment gateway is
-- not in Singapore.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is Overseas Spend` p MEANS
    NOT (p's currency EQUALS `Singapore dollars`)
    AND NOT (p's gateway EQUALS `A gateway in Singapore`)
    AND NOT (p's gateway EQUALS `Gateway not known`)

-- Petrol Spend: MCC 5541 or 5542; SPC and Shell are excluded by cl.1(iv)(c).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is Petrol Spend` p MEANS
    `the code is among` p (LIST 5541, 5542)

-- Contactless Transactions: tapped with the card or a wallet at a payWave
-- reader; Magnetic Secure Transmission is excluded; SimplyGo (ABT) fares count
-- from 1 July 2025.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a Contactless Transaction` p MEANS
    p's presentation EQUALS `Physical card tapped on a reader`
    OR p's presentation EQUALS `Wallet tapped on a reader`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a SimplyGo fare treated as Contactless` p MEANS
    p's merchant EQUALS `SimplyGo`
    AND p's item EQUALS `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`
    AND p's `date charged` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2025

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is in the Petrol and Contactless category` p MEANS
    `the purchase is Petrol Spend` p
    OR `the purchase is a Contactless Transaction` p
    OR `the purchase is a SimplyGo fare treated as Contactless` p


§§ `The arithmetic: UNI$10 per S$5 within the cap, UNI$1 beyond it`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Visa Signature minimum spend per category per statement period in S$` MEANS 1000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Visa Signature UNI$10 cap per category per statement period` MEANS 2400

-- UNI$1 = 2 miles (the programme's conversion, PRVI Miles T&C cl.1(i)).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`miles per UNI$ for the Visa Signature` MEANS 2

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS whole S$5 blocks in` amount MEANS
    FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 5)

-- How many whole blocks can still be paid at the UNI$10 rate under the cap.
GIVEN blocks IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS blocks that still earn UNI$10` blocks earned MEANS
    min blocks (FLOOR ((`at least nothing` (`the Visa Signature UNI$10 cap per category per statement period` MINUS earned)) DIVIDED BY 10))

-- Reading 1 (whole S$5 blocks): UNI$10 for each block under the cap, UNI$1 beyond it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS UNI$ by blocks` amount earned MEANS
    (`VS blocks that still earn UNI$10` (`VS whole S$5 blocks in` amount) earned) TIMES 10
    PLUS ((`VS whole S$5 blocks in` amount) MINUS (`VS blocks that still earn UNI$10` (`VS whole S$5 blocks in` amount) earned))

-- Reading 2 (pro rata): the same on fractional fives, rounded down once.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS fives at the UNI$10 rate` amount earned MEANS
    min (amount DIVIDED BY 5) ((`at least nothing` (`the Visa Signature UNI$10 cap per category per statement period` MINUS earned)) DIVIDED BY 10)

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS UNI$ pro rata` amount earned MEANS
    FLOOR ((`VS fives at the UNI$10 rate` amount earned) TIMES 10 PLUS ((amount DIVIDED BY 5) MINUS (`VS fives at the UNI$10 rate` amount earned)))

-- The basic tier alone: UNI$1 per whole S$5 (cl.1(i)); pro rata rounds the same.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS UNI$ at the basic rate` amount MEANS
    FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 5)

-- The bonus the blocks would earn before the cap: 9 per block.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS bonus UNI$ wanted` amount MEANS
    (`VS whole S$5 blocks in` amount) TIMES 9


§§ `The answer in one category`

-- The S$1,000 floor is a month-end condition: while the category's spend
-- including this purchase is under it, the bonus is not yet certain.
GIVEN spendSoFar IS A NUMBER
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the floor is met by` spendSoFar `with a purchase of` amount MEANS
    (spendSoFar PLUS amount) AT LEAST `the Visa Signature minimum spend per category per statement period in S$`

GIVEN spendSoFar IS A NUMBER
      amount IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`VS conditions for a spend so far of` spendSoFar `a purchase of` amount `and UNI$10 earned of` earned MEANS
    append (IF `the floor is met by` spendSoFar `with a purchase of` amount THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST `Visa Signature: the S$1,000 statement-period floor is reached`) (IF `VS UNI$ by blocks` amount earned EQUALS `VS UNI$ pro rata` amount earned THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      spendSoFar IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`VS certain UNI$` p spendSoFar earned MEANS
    IF `the floor is met by` spendSoFar `with a purchase of` (p's `amount in SGD`)
    THEN `VS UNI$ by blocks` (p's `amount in SGD`) earned
    ELSE `VS UNI$ at the basic rate` (p's `amount in SGD`)

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      spendSoFar IS A NUMBER
      earned IS A NUMBER
      thePot IS A Pot
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer in a category` c p spendSoFar earned thePot MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `UNI$` `of` (`VS certain UNI$` p spendSoFar earned) `to` (`VS UNI$ pro rata` (p's `amount in SGD`) earned) `wanting` (`VS bonus UNI$ wanted` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `at` (JUST `miles per UNI$ for the Visa Signature`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` thePot `depending on` (`VS conditions for a spend so far of` spendSoFar `a purchase of` (p's `amount in SGD`) `and UNI$10 earned of` earned) `per` "UOB Visa Signature T&C cl.2 ([NEW] block), cl.4(i)"

-- The ordinary basic tier, outside any category.
GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer at the basic tier` c p MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `UNI$` `of` (`VS UNI$ at the basic rate` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `to` (`VS UNI$ at the basic rate` (p's `amount in SGD`)) `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST `miles per UNI$ for the Visa Signature`) `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` EMPTY `per` "UOB Visa Signature T&C cl.1(i)"

GIVEN first IS AN `Earn answer`
      second IS AN `Earn answer`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the Visa Signature answer with fewer certain units` first second MEANS
    IF first's `units certain` AT MOST second's `units certain` THEN first ELSE second

GIVEN first IS AN `Earn answer`
      second IS AN `Earn answer`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the Visa Signature answer with more best units` first second MEANS
    IF first's `units at best` AT LEAST second's `units at best` THEN first ELSE second


§§ `The answer for one purchase`

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer in the overseas category` c p m MEANS
    `VS answer in a category` c p (m's `overseas spend`) (m's `overseas UNI$10 earned`) `Visa Signature overseas`

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer in the petrol and contactless category` c p m MEANS
    `VS answer in a category` c p (m's `contactless and petrol spend`) (m's `contactless and petrol UNI$10 earned`) `Visa Signature contactless and petrol`

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer when the code and gateway are settled` c p m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Visa Signature excludes the purchase` p
            THEN `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB Visa Signature T&C cl.1(iv)"
        IF `the purchase is Overseas Spend` p AND `the purchase is in the Petrol and Contactless category` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`the Visa Signature answer with fewer certain units` (`VS answer in the overseas category` c p m) (`VS answer in the petrol and contactless category` c p m)) `to` (`the Visa Signature answer with more best units` (`VS answer in the overseas category` c p m) (`VS answer in the petrol and contactless category` c p m)) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        IF `the purchase is Overseas Spend` p
            THEN `VS answer in the overseas category` c p m
        IF `the purchase is in the Petrol and Contactless category` p
            THEN `VS answer in the petrol and contactless category` c p m
        OTHERWISE `VS answer at the basic tier` c p

GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS earns nothing under the open reading` c MEANS
    `nothing is earned on` c `in` `UNI$` `per` "UOB Visa Signature T&C cl.1(iv)(a) (open reading)"

`a Visa Signature code that is excluded` MEANS 4829
`a Visa Signature code that earns` MEANS 5812

-- A foreign-currency online purchase whose gateway she cannot see is Overseas
-- Spend or local depending on it (cl.2(i)).
GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer at the worst gateway` c p m MEANS
    `VS answer when the code and gateway are settled` c (`rerouted purchase` p `A gateway in Singapore`) m

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer at the best gateway` c p m MEANS
    `VS answer when the code and gateway are settled` c (`rerouted purchase` p `A gateway in another country`) m

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`VS answer when the code is settled` c p m MEANS
    IF p's gateway EQUALS `Gateway not known` AND NOT (p's currency EQUALS `Singapore dollars`)
    THEN `bracketed from` (`VS answer at the worst gateway` c p m) `to` (`VS answer at the best gateway` c p m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant's payment gateway is not known`)
    ELSE `VS answer when the code and gateway are settled` c p m

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      m IS A `Visa Signature month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`UOB Visa Signature earns on` c p m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the code is unknown for` p
            THEN `bracketed from` (`VS answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a Visa Signature code that is excluded`) m) `to` (`VS answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a Visa Signature code that earns`) m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`)
        IF p's `charge kind` EQUALS `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`
            THEN `bracketed from` (`VS earns nothing under the open reading` c) `to` (`VS answer when the code is settled` c p m) `adding` (LIST `A reading of the text is open (see the fork register)`)
        OTHERWISE `VS answer when the code is settled` c p m


§§ `The clock the Visa Signature pots runs on`

-- cl.2 ("per statement period").
GIVETH A `Period basis`
`the Visa Signature pots' period` MEANS `Statement period`

GIVETH A `Date basis`
`the Visa Signature pots' date basis` MEANS `Not stated in the document`

#ASSERT `the Visa Signature pots' period` EQUALS `Statement period`
#ASSERT `the Visa Signature pots' date basis` EQUALS `Not stated in the document`


§§ `Illustrations`

`a Visa Signature` MEANS `UOB Visa Signature`

GIVEN localSpend IS A NUMBER
      localEarned IS A NUMBER
      overseasSpend IS A NUMBER
      overseasEarned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Visa Signature month`
`a Visa Signature month with` localSpend `of local spend,` localEarned `UNI$10 earned,` overseasSpend `of overseas spend and` overseasEarned `UNI$10 earned overseas` MEANS
    `Visa Signature month` WITH
        `contactless and petrol spend`         IS localSpend
        `contactless and petrol UNI$10 earned` IS localEarned
        `overseas spend`                       IS overseasSpend
        `overseas UNI$10 earned`               IS overseasEarned

`a fresh Visa Signature month` MEANS `a Visa Signature month with` 0 `of local spend,` 0 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`
`a Visa Signature month past the local floor` MEANS `a Visa Signature month with` 1000 `of local spend,` 2000 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`
`a Visa Signature month with the local cap spent` MEANS `a Visa Signature month with` 1200 `of local spend,` 2400 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`

`S$100 tapped with the physical card` MEANS `the base purchase`
`S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` MEANS `purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Wallet tapped on a reader`
`S$100 tapped with Samsung Pay by magnetic secure transmission` MEANS `purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Wallet by magnetic secure transmission`
`S$100 in an SGD online purchase` MEANS `purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Card number entered online`
`S$100 tapped overseas in yen` MEANS `purchase described as` (`rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` (`purchase at location` `the base purchase` `A store outside Singapore`) `Another foreign currency`) `A gateway in another country`) `Another description`
`S$100 online in US dollars through an overseas gateway` MEANS `purchase paid by` (`rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `A gateway in another country`) `Card number entered online`
`S$100 online in US dollars through a Singapore gateway` MEANS `purchase paid by` (`rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `A gateway in Singapore`) `Card number entered online`
`S$100 online in US dollars, gateway not known` MEANS `purchase paid by` (`rerouted purchase` (`purchase in currency` `the base purchase` `Another foreign currency`) `Gateway not known`) `Card number entered online`
`S$100 of petrol in Singapore dollars` MEANS `purchase paid by` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5541) `Physical card inserted or swiped`

-- cl.1(i): the basic tier outside any category: S$100 online in S$ earns UNI$20 = 40 miles.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 in an SGD online purchase` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- cl.2(iii): a tap earns UNI$10 per S$5 once the floor is met: S$100 -> 200 (400 miles).
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with the physical card` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT fromMaybe 0 ((`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with the physical card` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `miles certain`) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
-- ... but Magnetic Secure Transmission is not a payWave tap.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Samsung Pay by magnetic secure transmission` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- ... and the physical card tapped earns the same as a wallet (unlike the Preferred Visa).
-- The S$1,000 floor: S$100 on a fresh month cannot be certain of the bonus; floor 20, ceiling 200.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a fresh Visa Signature month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a fresh Visa Signature month`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT elem `Visa Signature: the S$1,000 statement-period floor is reached` ((`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a fresh Visa Signature month`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... the purchase that itself reaches S$1,000 makes it certain: S$900 so far + S$100 = S$1,000.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` (`a Visa Signature month with` 900 `of local spend,` 0 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
-- ... S$899.99 so far is not enough: the floor is still pending.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase for` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` 99.99) (`a Visa Signature month with` 900 `of local spend,` 0 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 19
-- The cap: UNI$2,400 of UNI$10 per category per statement period = S$1,200. With it spent, S$100 earns only UNI$20.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a Visa Signature month with the local cap spent`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- ... with UNI$2,300 earned, 10 blocks remain at UNI$10 (100 UNI$) and 10 blocks earn UNI$1 each: 110.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` (`a Visa Signature month with` 1150 `of local spend,` 2300 `UNI$10 earned,` 0 `of overseas spend and` 0 `UNI$10 earned overseas`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 110
-- The bonus wanted before the cap is 20 blocks x 9 = 180.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a Visa Signature month with the local cap spent`)'s `bonus units before cap` EQUALS 180
-- The pot named:
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s pot EQUALS `Visa Signature contactless and petrol`

-- cl.2(ii): petrol at MCC 5541 swiped is Petrol Spend.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 of petrol in Singapore dollars` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 of petrol in Singapore dollars` `Shell service station`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase at merchant` `S$100 of petrol in Singapore dollars` `SPC service station`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded

-- cl.2(i): overseas, separate floor and cap. A tap in yen overseas is Overseas Spend AND a Contactless Transaction:
-- the open reading F-vs-overlap. With both pots past their floor, both pay 200.
`a Visa Signature month with both floors met` MEANS `a Visa Signature month with` 1000 `of local spend,` 2000 `UNI$10 earned,` 1000 `of overseas spend and` 2000 `UNI$10 earned overseas`
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars through an overseas gateway` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars through an overseas gateway` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s pot EQUALS `Visa Signature overseas`
-- ... an overseas tap with only the local floor met: floor = the poorer pot (overseas, floor not met: 20), ceiling the richer (200).
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped overseas in yen` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 tapped overseas in yen` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 200
-- ... online in dollars through a Singapore gateway is not Overseas Spend: the basic tier.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars through a Singapore gateway` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
-- ... and when she does not know the gateway: floor basic 20, ceiling the overseas bonus 200.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars, gateway not known` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars, gateway not known` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT elem `The merchant's payment gateway is not known` ((`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `S$100 online in US dollars, gateway not known` `a Visa Signature month with both floors met`)'s `depends on`)

-- cl.2 (iii): SimplyGo (ABT) fares are Contactless Transactions from 1 July 2025.
`a SimplyGo fare of S$10 tapped with the card` MEANS `purchase for` (`purchase of item` (`purchase at merchant` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4111) `SimplyGo`) `A SimplyGo bus or train fare`) 10
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` `a SimplyGo fare of S$10 tapped with the card` `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase charged on` `a SimplyGo fare of S$10 tapped with the card` (Date 30 6 2025)) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 20

-- cl.4(i) and the per-five fork: S$4.99 tapped past the floor earns 0 on blocks and 9 pro rata (9.98 down).
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase for` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` 4.99) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase for` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` 4.99) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 9

-- cl.1(iv): what earns nothing.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `Bill payment`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`recoded purchase` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` 7523) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase described as` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `AXS`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase later reversed` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s excluded

-- A bill paid directly on the card: the open reading.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase of kind` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay` `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 200

-- The MCC not known: floor 0, ceiling the bonus.
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase with unknown code` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`UOB Visa Signature earns on` `a Visa Signature` (`purchase with unknown code` `S$100 tapped with Apple Pay`) `a Visa Signature month past the local floor`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 200
